You are executing the saas-multi-tenancy-architecture-spec skill. Your mandate is to produce a Multi_Tenancy_Architecture_Spec.md document plus a set of ADR seeds for a multi-tenant SaaS per Golding (2024) and IEEE 1016-2009 Sec 5.

1. Read SRS_Draft.md, HLD.md, tech_stack.md, PRD.md (if present), vision.md. Log all paths. Halt if SRS_Draft.md or HLD.md is missing. Identify regulatory constraints (HIPAA, PCI-DSS, GDPR, POPIA, SOC2, ISO 27001, DPPA), data-residency obligations, target ICP segments, and tier mix.
2. Produce the Two-Plane Decomposition. Generate a Mermaid flowchart showing the control plane (onboarding, identity, tenant management, metering, billing, deployment automation, operations console) and the application plane (domain microservices). Every node SHALL have a descriptive label. Classify every in-scope service as control-plane or application-plane.
3. Fill the Per-Microservice Tenancy-Pattern Matrix. For each application-plane microservice, choose one of {Full-Stack Silo, Full-Stack Pool, Mixed-Mode, Pod, Account-per-Tenant/VPC-per-Tenant}. State drivers (regulatory, isolation, blast-radius, cost, performance, noisy-neighbor) with measurable thresholds. State trade-offs accepted. Reference an ADR seed filename.
4. Write the Tenant Context Specification. Define token format (recommend signed JWT with claims: tenant_id, tier, region, roles, issuer, expiry), issuance (control-plane Identity service), propagation (HTTP header X-Tenant-Context or gRPC metadata or async-event envelope), validation at each service boundary, and fail-safe behaviour when missing or invalid (reject 401/403, audit log entry, alert). Cite SRS clauses.
5. Write the Isolation Strategy. For every pooled service, document isolation at: network (VPC/subnet/security groups/service mesh), compute (process/container/namespace/throttling), storage (database/schema/row-level security/per-tenant KMS), IAM (role-per-tenant or attribute-based), code path (tenant-aware repository helpers, lint rules, runtime assertions). Reference enforcement evidence.
6. Document Noisy-Neighbor controls and Per-Tier SLOs. For every pooled service: rate limit per tenant per tier, quotas, per-tier SLO (Bronze/Silver/Gold/Enterprise) for availability, latency P95, support response time. Define burst headroom and back-off.
7. Document Per-Tenant Cost Attribution. For every pooled service: metering events emitted, granularity, allocation of shared costs, reporting destination (FinOps + ERP), cadence. Cross-link to the Billing & Metering SRS.
8. Emit ADR seeds. For each microservice generate adr-seeds/0001-tenancy-pattern-<service>.md using the saas-tenancy-decision-template.md format. Emit adr-seeds/0002-control-plane-boundary.md.
9. Write Multi_Tenancy_Architecture_Spec.md with sections: 1) Two-Plane Decomposition, 2) Control-Plane Services Inventory, 3) Application-Plane Services Inventory, 4) Per-Microservice Tenancy-Pattern Matrix, 5) Tenant Context Specification, 6) Isolation Strategy, 7) Noisy-Neighbor & Per-Tier SLOs, 8) Per-Tenant Cost Attribution, 9) Tenant Lifecycle Event Catalogue, 10) Document Numbering Design (single allocator, document type register, tenant and platform series, issue events, void path, idempotency, offline provisional tags, gap report; per `../../02-requirements-engineering/references/document-numbering-requirements.md` section 8), 11) ADR Seed Index, 12) Traceability Matrix. Log section count and ADR seed count.

Validation: Halt if any application-plane microservice has no tenancy-pattern row. Halt if any pooled service lacks a noisy-neighbor control or per-tier SLO. Halt if tenant-context spec lacks a fail-safe rule. Halt if the traceability matrix has any row without an SRS or PRD identifier. Halt if the system issues numbered documents and the Document Numbering Design section is missing or names more than one number generator.
